# Optional settings for the trading journal.
#
# To use any of these: copy this file to ".env" in the same folder, uncomment
# the lines you want, and restart with `npm start`. Works the same on Windows,
# macOS and Linux, so you never have to fight your shell's syntax.
#
# The .env file is gitignored and stays on your machine.


# Which port to serve on. Change it if 4317 is already taken.
# PORT=4317


# Where your journal is stored: the database, chart screenshots and backups.
# Defaults to the "data" folder inside this project.
#
# Point it at a synced folder to keep everything backed up off-machine. Note
# that Google Drive must be set to "Mirror files" rather than streaming for
# this to be safe. Dropbox and iCloud mirror by default.
#
# Windows:  JOURNAL_DATA_DIR=C:\Users\YourName\Dropbox\TradingJournal
# macOS:    JOURNAL_DATA_DIR=/Users/yourname/Dropbox/TradingJournal
#
# JOURNAL_DATA_DIR=


# Where backups go, if you want them somewhere other than alongside the data.
#
# This is the safer way to use a cloud drive: the live database stays on real
# local disk, and only the backup copies sync. Recommended over the setting
# above if you are unsure.
#
# Windows:  JOURNAL_BACKUP_DIR=C:\Users\YourName\My Drive\TradingJournalBackups
# macOS:    JOURNAL_BACKUP_DIR=/Users/yourname/Google Drive/My Drive/TradingJournalBackups
#
# JOURNAL_BACKUP_DIR=
